<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A1.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracy across datasets and query variants (LLaMA-3.1-8B).<span id="A1.T6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report accuracy for original queries, synthetically generated paraphrased queries, and paraphrased queries with fixed retrieval. Across all settings, accuracy remains relatively similar, indicating that paraphrasing and retrieval shifts have limited effect on final answer correctness on average. See result for <span id="A1.T6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen-2.5-3B</span> model in Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.3 LLM-Judge Consistency Evaluation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Improving Consistency in Retrieval-Augmented Systems with Group Similarity Rewards" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
